{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the pillars of the court all around, and their sockets, and their pegs, and their cords</b> — of the pillars, for the pegs and cords of the hangings were in the charge of the sons of Gershon. There were pegs and cords for the curtains and for the hangings below, so that the wind would not lift them, and there were pegs and cords for the pillars all around, to hang the hangings from them at their upper edge by means of poles and rods, as we learned in the craft of the Tabernacle — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 4:32). But I do not know what pegs would do for the pillars, and furthermore what distinguishes the pegs of the pillars from the rest of the pegs, that these belong to the sons of Gershon and those to the sons of Merari. And I have not found in the Mishnah of the craft of the Tabernacle that there were pegs for the pillars; rather, this is what we learned there (chapter 5): He would connect the rods with the cords and with the pillars, and connect them within the pegs of the Tent. And just as there were pegs for the Tabernacle, so there were pegs for the court, as it is stated (Exodus 27:19): \"for all the vessels of the Tabernacle in all its service, and all its pegs, and all the pegs of the court (around), copper\" — this is the language of the Baraita, and it did not teach there that there are pegs for the pillars. Rather, let us explain that the pegs and cords of the hangings of the court were in the hands of the sons of Merari, while the cords and pegs of the Tabernacle and the Tent are those that were in the hands of the sons of Gershon. For \"and their cords and all their service vessels\" (Numbers 4:26) is a designation referring to the curtains of the Tabernacle and to the Tent of Meeting that are mentioned at the beginning of the verse (Numbers 4:25), not to the court. And so he said above (3:26), \"and its cords,\" which is an allusion to the Tabernacle that is mentioned there (verse 25), not to the hangings of the court. And similar to this is \"but they shall not come near the holy vessels and the altar\" (Numbers 18:3), which refers to \"your father's tribe\" — the distant one, not to \"your sons\" — the near one. And likewise \"and its redemption from a month old you shall redeem\" (ibid. verse 16) refers back to \"the firstborn of man,\" not to \"the firstborn of unclean animals,\" and so many others. But according to the language of the Baraita, it appears to me that the sons of Gershon carried nothing but textiles — no copper or wood at all. And this is what we learned (there chapter 13): \"The sons of Gershon were stationed on the west, and they are appointed over the woven implements.\" If so, the meaning of <b>their pegs</b> would be those of the Tabernacle and of the pillars of the court, and <b>their cords</b> those of the pillars of the court alone. And so he said above (3:36): \"the planks of the Tabernacle and its bars and its pillars and its sockets and all its vessels and all its service,\" and this would include its pegs. And therefore he mentions cords for both of them but does not mention pegs except for the sons of Merari." "And the reason for <b>and by name you shall count the vessels of the charge of their burden</b> is that he should entrust into the hand of each man, by an individual list of names, the vessels of his burden according to their count. That is to say: \"So-and-so shall carry from the planks such-and-such a number, and so-and-so from the bars or the pillars such-and-such a number\" — not that he would command: \"The sons of Merari collectively shall carry all the planks and the sockets and the pillars.\" And he mentioned this first concerning the sons of Merari because of the heaviness of their burden, lest each one lighten his own burden and cast it upon his fellow. And the same rule applies also to the sons of Kohath and Gershon."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Ramban cites the Baraita of Mekhilta de-Milluim (chapter 13), known as מלאכת המשכן, a rabbinic source detailing the construction of the Tabernacle."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:55.260657942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}